Prompt: Create an artwork depicting a landing page layout for an exhibition titled “Tradition and Transformation: Unlinear; Medieval Era to the Photorealism Era”. The main subject matter of this design should be Medieval Art. The landing page must show Medieval-era artworks such as The Ladder of Divine Ascent and The Annunciation with Saint Margaret and Saint Ansanus. The design should clearly contrast the religious hierarchy in the Medieval artwork with modern social injustices, using a photorealistic style. The concepts should clash as the photorealism curates a 3D effect in the artwork, contrary to the traditional flat textures of medieval art pieces. Include negative shapes that are non-linear, with no strict shapes, to help guide the user throughout the landing page.
Chosen Themes: Medieval Sacred Art vs Freedom & Liberation
Vocabulary: Contemporary Art: Art of the present time, but one could argue that we have lost the value of previous meaning to the early 20th century of contemporary art with digital media
Photorealism: 2D art done so well that it looks 3D or like a photo. 
Directional Lines: Commonly found in almost all types of artwork, as this can guide the viewer to a larger meaning of an art piece.
Value Contrast: Can be negative or positive contrasts but are typically parallel and in grayscale.
Focal Point: Where the viewer or artist holds their attention in their art piece, or the main point of an art piece.
